diff --git a/docs/user/advanced.rst b/docs/user/advanced.rst
--- a/docs/user/advanced.rst
+++ b/docs/user/advanced.rst
@@ -1058,6 +1058,17 @@ time out unless a timeout value is set explicitly. Without a timeout, your code
 may hang for minutes or more.
 
+Sessions can provide a mutable default timeout for calls where ``timeout`` is
+omitted::
+
+    s = requests.Session()
+    s.default_timeout = 5
+    r = s.get('https://github.com')
+
+The session default is used only when the ``timeout`` argument is omitted.
+Passing ``timeout=None`` explicitly overrides the session default and disables
+the timeout for that request.
+
 The **connect** timeout is the number of seconds Requests will wait for your
 client to establish a connection to a remote machine (corresponding to the
 `connect()`_) call on the socket. It's a good practice to set connect timeouts
